        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): reject loose click coordinate numbers when normalizing actions",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Browser action requests could accept loose coordinate numbers for `clickCoords`, such as hexadecimal or exponent-form strings, when users or tools submit direct coordinate clicks through the browser `/act` workflow.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`clickCoords` now uses browser-owned decimal-only finite coordinate parsing before dispatch, matching the existing Browser schema and CLI contract that allow fractional CSS-pixel coordinates while rejecting non-decimal numeric syntax. This is an owner-local browser route normalization fix only; it does not add config, compatibility aliases, or provider behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBrowser action callers get consistent validation for coordinate clicks: decimal and fractional coordinates continue to work, while hexadecimal and exponent-form strings are rejected before a click is dispatched.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: Browser `/act` route normalization preserves decimal and fractional `clickCoords` coordinates, rejects loose numeric strings, and does not dispatch malformed coordinate clicks.\n- Current PR head: `31a4da266410c811419e3d2d2089f5da1c25d28c` with tree `8fd4782486b7012d911a12cb47be458d0f7e2d19`; focused proof below ran in `D:\\work_project\\openclaw-lane-c` on the matching tree `8fd4782486b7012d911a12cb47be458d0f7e2d19`.\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.act.normalize.test.ts` passed with 10 tests passing.\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-core.test.ts --testNamePattern \"malformed coordinate clicks|navigation \\+ common act commands\"` passed with 2 tests passing and 21 skipped.\n  - `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` passed.\n  - `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode local` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Observed result: normalization accepts decimal fractional strings such as `x: \"10.5\", y: \".25\"`; the `/act` route forwards fractional `x: \"42.5\"` to the Playwright click path as `42.5`; and `/act` returns `ACT_INVALID_REQUEST` with `clickCoords requires non-negative x and y` for negative, hexadecimal, and exponent-form coordinate inputs without invoking `clickCoordsViaPlaywright`.",
        "branch": "codex/fix-browser-clickcoords-strict-numbers",
